# nr-office-author-pptx-charts: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own).
# (No protocol rows, no daemon service, no SERVICE_PENDING change, no Cargo edge: the chart writer and the normaliser are
# library modules of mixdog-office-author; every crate they use (mixdog-ooxml, mixdog-js, mixdog-fsio, mixdog-office-base,
# serde_json; dev: base64, mixdog-office-base with test-support) is in the crate's Cargo.toml already. The callers are the
# pptx build task (nr-office-author-pptx-build) and the script runner (nr-office-author-script-runtime).)

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/src/lib.rs
Add the module beside `pub mod geometry;` (any place in the list; it has no dependency on the others):

    pub mod normalize;

and one line to the crate's header comment: `normalize`, the post-processing of an authored deck (`authoring/pptx-script-normalize.mjs`:
one `a:pPr` per paragraph, merged accent series, chart faces, schema order, native gradients, unique shape ids, icon SVGs,
the presentation's list order).

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/src/pptx_writer/mod.rs
Beside `mod media;` add (alphabetical: before `media`):

    mod chart_workbook;
    mod charts;

and beside `pub use media::ImageFile;` add:

    pub use charts::{AxisCrossing, AxisStyle, Chart, ChartArea, ChartBorder, ChartData, ChartKind, ChartLayout, ChartOptions, ChartShadow, GridLine, PlotArea, TitlePos};

In the module comment, "Not carried" gains: the 3D bar, the bubble chart and combo charts with a secondary axis (the chart
writer of charts.rs carries area, bar and column, line, pie, doughnut, radar and scatter).

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/src/pptx_writer/slide.rs  (a chart is one of the slide's objects)
(a) imports: `use super::charts::{Chart, ChartData, ChartKind, ChartOptions};`

(b) `enum SlideObject`: add the variant `Chart(Chart),` after `Image(ImageObject),`.

(c) `Slide::next_rel_id` (`getNewRelId`): the chart relationships count too:

    fn next_rel_id(&self) -> usize {
        self.rels.len() + self.rels_media.len() + self.charts().count() + 1
    }

and beside it:

    /// The charts of the slide in the order they were added (`slide._relsChart`).
    pub(crate) fn charts(&self) -> impl Iterator<Item = &Chart> {
        self.objects.iter().filter_map(|object| match object {
            SlideObject::Chart(chart) => Some(chart),
            _ => None,
        })
    }

    /// `slide.addChart(type, data, options)`; `id` is the deck's chart number (`Presentation::add_chart` counts them).
    pub(crate) fn add_chart(&mut self, kind: ChartKind, data: Vec<ChartData>, options: ChartOptions, id: usize) -> Result<(), String> {
        let before = self.charts().count();
        let chart = Chart::new(kind, data, options, id, self.next_rel_id(), before)?;
        self.objects.push(SlideObject::Chart(chart));
        Ok(())
    }

(d) `csld_xml`, in the `match object` of the loop over `input.objects`, add:

    SlideObject::Chart(chart) => xml.push_str(&chart.frame_xml(index, input.layout)),

(e) `Slide::rels_xml`: after the loop over `self.rels` and before the loop over `self.rels_media` (the order of
`slideObjectRelationsToXml`: hyperlinks, charts, media) add:

    for chart in self.charts() {
        last = last.max(chart.rid());
        xml.push_str(&format!("<Relationship Id=\"rId{}\" Type=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/chart\" Target=\"{}\"/>", chart.rid(), chart.target()));
    }

(`SlideObject` derives Debug, Clone, PartialEq; `Chart` derives the same. `notes_text` and the picture and shape counters
already match on their own variants only, so a chart does not change them: a chart's id on the slide is its place among
the slide's objects plus 2, as for the others.)

## 4. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/src/pptx_writer/presentation.rs
(a) `struct Presentation`: a field `chart_counter: usize,` (pptxgenjs's module-level `_chartCounter`, here one per deck:
`chart<n>.xml` numbers from 1), initialised to 0 in `Presentation::new` (and `Default` if it is spelled out).
Imports: `use super::charts::{ChartData, ChartKind, ChartOptions};`

(b) beside `add_slide`:

    /// `slide.addChart(type, data, options)` on the slide at `index`.
    pub fn add_chart(&mut self, index: usize, kind: ChartKind, data: Vec<ChartData>, options: ChartOptions) -> Result<(), String> {
        self.chart_counter += 1;
        let id = self.chart_counter;
        let slide = self.slides.get_mut(index).ok_or_else(|| format!("no slide {index}"))?;
        slide.add_chart(kind, data, options, id)
    }

(c) `content_types_xml`: the loop `for index in 1..=self.slides.len()` that writes the slide master and slide overrides
becomes a loop over `self.slides.iter().enumerate()` (`index` is `at + 1`), and after the slide's Override it adds, as
`makeXmlContTypes` does, for each chart of the slide:

    for chart in slide.charts() {
        xml.push_str(&format!("<Override PartName=\"{}\" ContentType=\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.drawingml.chart+xml\"/>", chart.target()));
    }

(The `xlsx` Default is already written there.)

(d) `package`: after the loop that writes the media of every slide (pptxgenjs writes the media synchronously and each chart's
parts when its workbook is generated, so charts come after all media), add:

    for slide in &self.slides {
        for chart in slide.charts() {
            for (name, bytes) in chart.parts()? {
                package.set(&name, bytes);
            }
        }
    }

(`FOLDERS` already holds `ppt/charts`, `ppt/charts/_rels` and `ppt/embeddings`: the folder entries are written first.)

