## 6. For the later tasks of the track
The new exports: `pptx_writer::{Chart, ChartData, ChartKind, ChartOptions, AxisStyle, ChartShadow, ...}` (the options of
`addChart` by their pptxgenjs names in snake case; an unset option is `None`/`false`, as `undefined` is), `Presentation::add_chart(slide_index,
kind, data, options)`, `Chart::{new, xml, parts, rels_xml, target, frame_xml}`; and `normalize::{normalize_authored_pptx(proof,
note, path), normalize_package(&mut Package), Normalized, merge_accent_series, order_chart_children, native_gradients,
gradient_fill_xml, unique_shape_ids, normalize_chart_fonts, prune_undeclared_axis_ids, order_presentation_lists,
normalize_paragraph_properties}`. The caller of the build (nr-office-author-pptx-build) runs `normalize_authored_pptx` on the
saved deck, as `pptx-script-runner.mjs` and `pptx-html-runner.mjs` do.
Kept on purpose: the colour of a marker past the colour list is random (`Math.random` of pptxgenjs, `mixdog_js::math::random`),
and so are the identifiers of a scatter chart's custom labels. Not carried: 3D bar, bubble, combo charts with a secondary axis.

## Not compiled
The modules were written without cargo (the wave is compiled by the lead): `cargo test -p mixdog-office-author` is the check
(unit tests in charts.rs, chart_workbook.rs and normalize.rs, the ten tests of `pptx-script-normalize.test.mjs` among
them; tests/twin_pptx_charts.rs replays native/core/fixtures/office-author-pptx-charts and needs no Node;
`twin_live_pptx_charts` (ignored) re-records through Node). The twin test needs the two `mod` lines and the `pub use` of
section 2 and `pub mod normalize` of section 1; the chart replay does not need sections 3 and 4.
